INSERT INTO "mission_offers" VALUES('mon_consultant_independant','db1aba12b52e64a6','Directeur de projet - migration de ECC vers S/4HANA','https://www.mon-consultant-independant.com/missions-consultants-freelance',NULL,'Paris et région parisienne',600,600,'2j télétravail / semaine','6 mois',NULL,'Pour un client du secteur du transport, recherche d''**un Directeur de Projet SAP Finance**, ayant déjà mené des cadrages avec définition des règles de Gouvernance, cadrage puis pilotage du projet de migration vers S/4 HANA','','2026-08-21T06:15:00+00:00','2026-08-31T06:15:00+00:00','2026-09-07T11:03:33+00:00','withdrawn',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "mission_offers" VALUES('mon_consultant_independant','9afd9f8db5ecd4bb','Senior consultant carbon footprint and financed emissions','https://www.mon-consultant-independant.com/missions-consultants-freelance',NULL,'Luxembourg',899,899,'2j télétravail / semaine','6 mois',NULL,'For an international banking institution, we are looking for a **senior independent consultant specialising in Carbon Footprint, Climate Risk and Financed Emissions**. The assignment aims to support the bank in strengthening its carbon accounting framework, with a particular focus on **Scope 3 financed emissions**, and in meeting European banking regulatory and prudential expectations relating to climate and ESG risks. ** The consultant will notably be expected to : ** - assess the bank’s existing carbon footprint framework, methodologies, data and governance; - define the appropriate organisational and operational perimeter for the carbon footprint assessment; - review and, where required, calculate **Scope 1 and Scope 2 emissions**; - assess the materiality of the different **Scope 3 categories** applicable to the bank; - focus specifically on **Scope 3 Category 15 – Investments / Financed Emissions**; - map the bank’s lending and investment portfolios to the relevant carbon accounting methodologies and asset classes; - calculate financed emissions for relevant portfolios, including Corporate lending, Large Corporate exposures, Project Finance, bonds, commercial real estate and other material investments; - apply recognised methodologies, notably the **GHG Protocol and PCAF – Partnership for Carbon Accounting Financials**; - collect and structure counterparty, exposure, financial and carbon-emission data; - calculate absolute financed emissions and relevant carbon-intensity indicators; - assess data availability, coverage and quality, including **PCAF data-quality scoring**; - develop documented proxy and estimation methodologies where counterparty carbon data is unavailable; - identify the main carbon-intensive sectors, portfolios and counterparties; - analyse the main drivers of financed-emission levels and changes over time; - define appropriate carbon and climate-related KPIs and KRIs; - support the integration of climate metrics into credit risk management, portfolio monitoring, risk appetite, ICAAP and climate risk management; - contribute to the enhancement of ESG questionnaires used during credit origination and annual credit reviews; - assess the consistency of the carbon footprint methodology with relevant **CSSF, EBA and European banking prudential requirements**; - support the preparation of relevant **Pillar 3 ESG disclosures and climate-related regulatory reporting**; - establish appropriate reconciliations with Finance, Credit Risk and regulatory reporting data; - define data governance, controls, data lineage and audit trails; - prepare methodological, procedural and regulatory documentation; - develop management and senior management reporting dashboards; - propose a roadmap to improve carbon-data coverage, reliability and automation; - train and transfer knowledge to the bank’s Risk, Credit, Finance, Sustainability and Regulatory Reporting teams. The consultant must have significant experience in **banking, carbon accounting, climate risk and financed emissions**, with proven hands-on experience in calculating the carbon footprint of lending or investment portfolios. Previous experience with **PCAF, GHG Protocol, Scope 3 Category 15, Pillar 3 ESG reporting and European banking regulatory requirements** is strongly preferred. A good understanding of banking credit portfolios, Corporate and Project Finance exposures, ESG risk management and prudential reporting is essential. Experience with data management and quantitative tools such as **advanced Excel, SQL, Python and/or Power BI** would be highly valued. The assignment will be performed in an international environment. **Professional fluency in English and French is mandatory.**','','2026-08-21T06:15:00+00:00','2026-08-31T06:15:00+00:00','2026-09-07T11:03:33+00:00','withdrawn',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "mission_offers" VALUES('mon_consultant_independant','d3a0549e2ad37de1','Senior consultant ECL IFRS 9 model validation','https://www.mon-consultant-independant.com/missions-consultants-freelance',NULL,'Luxembourg',999,999,'2j télétravail / semaine','6 mois',NULL,'For an international banking institution, we are looking for a **senior independent consultant specialising in IFRS 9 and Expected Credit Loss ECL model validation.** The assignment aims to **support the bank in the justification**, validation and backtesting of a Group ECL model used for a Corporate portfolio, for which some detailed parameters and methodological components are not directly accessible to the local entity. ** The consultant will notably be expected to : ** - assess the existing ECL framework and identify its main limitations; - evaluate the relevance and adequacy of the model for the Corporate portfolio concerned; - review the main ECL components including PD, LGD, EAD, CCF, staging, SICR, forward-looking macroeconomic scenarios and management overlays; - define and perform backtesting of PD, LGD, EAD and ECL outputs; - compare model estimates with observed defaults, recoveries and realised losses; - design and perform sensitivity, stability and consistency tests; - develop independent challenger approaches to assess the reasonableness of the Group model outputs; - use, where relevant, external data such as external ratings, default statistics, CDS spreads, bond spreads, secondary market prices of syndicated loans and borrower financial information; - assess the representativeness of the model development population compared with the European portfolio; - propose documented adjustments or management overlays where necessary; - contribute to the definition of a sustainable local model validation and governance framework; - prepare documentation supporting discussions with control functions, auditors and supervisory authorities; - contribute to a regulatory remediation plan aimed at demonstrating the robustness of the ECL framework and addressing existing supervisory findings. The consultant **must have significant experience in banking credit risk, IFRS 9 and model validation, ideally covering Corporate or Large Corporate portfolios.** Previous experience in validating Group models, vendor models or partially black-box models, as well as a strong understanding of European banking supervisory expectations, would be highly valued. The consultant will work with 2 quantitative analysts of the Bank. Experience with quantitative tools such as Python, SAS, R, SQL or advanced Excel is desirable. The assignment will be performed in an international environment. Professional fluency in English and French is mandatory.','','2026-08-21T06:15:00+00:00','2026-08-29T06:15:00+00:00','2026-08-30T06:15:01+00:00','withdrawn',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "mission_offers" VALUES('mon_consultant_independant','98d189950a011eb4','Consultant senior – transformation comptable','https://www.mon-consultant-independant.com/missions-consultants-freelance',NULL,'Paris et région parisienne',700,700,'100% présentiel','6 mois',NULL,'Pour le compte d’un acteur majeur du secteur bancaire, nous recherchons **un(e) consultant(e) expérimenté(e) (+10 ans d’exp)**. ** La mission vise à accompagner la transformation d’activités de comptabilité : ** · Vous interviendrez sur un programme structurant de sécurisation, d’harmonisation et d’optimisation des processus comptables. · Vos travaux débuteront par le cadrage du dispositif, la cartographie des processus et l’identification des tâches critiques. · Vous confirmerez les périmètres d''activités à transférer : les volumes, charges et impacts organisationnels associés. · Vous formaliserez les rôles et responsabilités entre direction financière, directions métiers et fonctions de contrôle. · Vous contribuerez à la préparation de la bascule : RACI, procédures, habilitations, SLA et contrôles de niveau 1. · Vous piloterez également le suivi des suspens, des écritures manuelles et des indicateurs de performance. Une attention particulière sera portée à la conduite du changement et à la mobilisation des équipes concernées. Nous recherchons un profil disposant d’une solide expérience en transformation de la fonction finance. Une excellente maîtrise de la comptabilité générale, des contrôles comptables et des environnements bancaires est attendue. Rigueur, autonomie, capacité de structuration et aisance relationnelle seront déterminantes pour réussir. Démarrage souhaité mi-septembre 2026.','','2026-08-21T06:15:00+00:00','2026-08-29T06:15:00+00:00','2026-08-30T06:15:01+00:00','withdrawn',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "mission_offers" VALUES('mon_consultant_independant','8d40d39841a5dcfc','Consultant production reporting réglementaire solvabilité (RWA, Risque de crédit)','https://www.mon-consultant-independant.com/missions-consultants-freelance',NULL,'Paris et région parisienne',718,718,'2j télétravail / semaine','9 mois',NULL,'** Contexte : ** pour un client bancaire nous recherchons un profil pour renforcer le dispositif en charge de la production des reportings prudentiels. Ce renfort intervient dans le cadre de l''internalisation d''un consultant ** Profil recherché : ** Profil expérimenté sur la Solvabilité : production et pilotage RWA, reporting COREP. Connaissances souhaitées principalement sur la dimension Crédit. Les dimensions Risque Op / CVA / Marché sont un plus. ** Compétences recherchées : ** · Production des RWA et ratios Solvabilité · Contrôles de cohérence métier · Analyse des variations trimestrielles / annuelles · Production des rapports COREP crédit · Production de synthèses à destination des comités de validation Solvabilité · Restitutions aux lignes métiers, aux lignes de contrôle, etc. · Contribution aux projets d''évolution de la chaine prudentielle (hors périodes d''arrêté) · Connaissance des outils Moodys Analytics, Dataiku et Qlik Sense sont un plus. ** Séniorité : ** minimum 6-8 ans, dont une expérience opérationnelle significative en production sur un périmètre similaire et une profondeur d''expertise normative/méthodologique sur les thématiques listées ci-dessus','','2026-08-21T06:15:00+00:00','2026-08-28T06:15:00+00:00','2026-08-29T06:15:00+00:00','withdrawn',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
