INSERT INTO "mission_offers" VALUES('emagine','319173','TMS Application & Configuration Manager','https://portal.emagine.org/jobs/180141',NULL,'Poland',NULL,NULL,'Remote','4-6 mois','ASAP','PROJECT INFORMATION: Start: ASAP (flexible). Rate: depending on experience. Contract: B2B 6 months + prolongations. Remote: up to 100% Location: remote Project language: English. Recruitment process: 1-2 interviews. Assignment Description: The TMS Application & Configuration Manager will be responsible for owning the functional configuration and day-to-day application management of the Transport Management System. This role encompasses configuration ownership, managing change requests, supporting rollouts, and providing operational support. The consultant will work closely with various stakeholders and serve as the primary point of contact for application-related tasks. Main Responsibilities: Manage functional configuration and application integration of the Transport Management System. Oversee change requests and coordinate enhancements through to testing and go-live. Support the rollout of the system across different countries and business units. Act as the main liaison with the technology and operational teams. Ensure maintenance of the Group template while adapting to local needs. Key Requirements: Minimum of 5 years’ experience with Transport Management Systems. Ability to manage multi-country business applications. Strong knowledge of logistics, transportation, and supply chain processes. Experience in configuring workflows and managing data structures in enterprise applications. Proficient analytical, problem-solving, and communication skills. Nice to Have: Experience with CarLo/Soloplan is preferred. Familiarity with SQL, EDI/API integrations. Experience working with diverse stakeholders in a multi-stakeholder environment. Other Details: This position is fully remote and offers a minimum project duration of 6 months, with the possibility of a 12-month extension. The consultant will engage in extensive direct interaction with various Business Owners to facilitate coordination and optimize application performance.','','2026-09-12T06:15:00+00:00','2026-09-13T06:15:00+00:00',NULL,'seen',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "mission_offers" VALUES('emagine','319192','Développeur Androïd/KMP Senior - (h/f)','https://portal.emagine.org/jobs/180140',NULL,'Lyon, France',NULL,NULL,'Hybrid','7-9 mois','01.10.2026','Nous recherchons un Développeur Androïd/KMP Senior, créatif et passionné par le code de qualité, pour rejoindre l’équipe de notre client. Ce rôle se concentre sur la rédaction d''un code propre et sécurisé, ainsi que sur la production de solutions de paiement numérique qui favorisent la croissance économique durable. Responsabilités principales Écriture d''un code propre et sécurisé selon les principes de Clean Architecture. Production de code réutilisable. Accompagnement des nouveaux développeurs et fourniture d''un support technique continu. Création et conception de prototypes exploitables. Application des normes et outils de conception appropriés. Collaboration avec d''autres spécialistes IT pour livrer des solutions logicielles. Exigences clés Minimum 5 ans d''expérience en développement mobile en Kotlin et Jetpack Compose. Maîtrise des concepts de développement assisté par IA. Expérience avec Git/GitLab. Connaissance des outils modernes d''Android (Android Studio, Maven, Gradle, etc.). Solides compétences en conception et développement logiciel. Excellentes capacités d''analyse et de résolution de problèmes. Compétences organisationnelles et gestion du temps. Maîtrise de l''anglais, à l''oral comme à l''écrit. Atouts souhaités Connaissance des technologies Compose Multiplatform / Kotlin Multiplatform. Aptitudes pédagogiques pour accompagner l''intégration des nouveaux collègues. Expérience de travail en mode Agile et workflow GitFlow. Détails supplémentaires Début de la mission : 01.10.2026 Durée de la mission : mission longue (7 à 9 mois) Localisation : Lyon Télétravail : possible','','2026-09-12T06:15:00+00:00','2026-09-13T06:15:00+00:00',NULL,'seen',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "mission_offers" VALUES('emagine','319190','Senior QA Lead / Test Manager – WMS Integration (Short-Term)','https://portal.emagine.org/jobs/180139',NULL,'Brazil',NULL,NULL,'Remote','4-6 mois','01.10.2026','Introduction & Summary: This role seeks an experienced Senior QA Lead with expertise in testing governance, specifically in a supply chain and WMS integration environment. The successful candidate will bring prior Manhattan WMS testing experience and be comfortable leading across multiple stakeholders, ensuring quality delivery throughout the project lifecycle. Main Responsibilities: Oversee testing governance across a three-way integration involving multiple systems. Define test strategy and build comprehensive test plans. Establish entry and exit criteria for testing phases. Lead System Integration Testing (SIT), User Acceptance Testing (UAT), regression, cutover, and hypercare activities. Coordinate with business, IT, and vendors to ensure alignment. Manage defect triage processes and report status to project leadership. Key Requirements: Prior Manhattan WMS testing experience . Background in supply chain / WMS integration testing . Ability to own governance and coordinate with stakeholders. Experience in functional and performance testing . Other Details: The project timeline involves contract negotiations now, design and mapping starting early October, with key phases extending through to mid-February 2026.','','2026-09-12T06:15:00+00:00','2026-09-13T06:15:00+00:00',NULL,'seen',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "mission_offers" VALUES('emagine','319189','Ingénieur Data Python AWS (h/f)','https://portal.emagine.org/jobs/180138',NULL,'Île-de-France, France',NULL,NULL,'Hybrid','> 12 mois','15.10.2026','Résumé Un poste d''ingénieur data est ouvert au sein d''une organisation axée sur les données, visant à maximiser l''exploitation des données pour développer de nouvelles offres, réduire les risques opérationnels et améliorer l''efficacité de l''équipe afin de mieux servir les clients. Responsabilités Construire et améliorer le cadre commun (composants fonctionnels et techniques). Supporter le déploiement de la MDM dans différents pays. Concevoir et mettre en œuvre des composants de la plateforme tels que l''ingestion et le traitement des données. Distribuer les données aux différentes parties prenantes. Assurer la conformité avec les directives du groupe concernant l''utilisation des cadres internes et l''architecture. Collaborer avec d''autres parties prenantes du projet pour promouvoir des lignes directrices communes. Collecter, comprendre et affiner les exigences commerciales. Concevoir des solutions en suivant les directives d''architecture. Participer aux activités de développement en tant que rôle senior/expert. Écrire et mettre à jour la documentation technique en anglais. Communiquer efficacement avec toutes les équipes concernées. Compétences Requises Ingénierie logicielle : Design & Architecture logicielle, Python, Programmation Orientée Objet. Architecture des données : architecture en couches, solutions de stockage et d''exposition. Technologies Big Data : pipelines de données, HDFS/S3/Parquet. Modèles de Big Data : partitionnement, indexation, optimisation des requêtes. Compétences AWS : sécurité/IAM, S3, Lambda. Compétences Appréciées Expérience en ingénierie des données. Compétences sur les structures de données / modélisation des données & SQL. Compréhension des processus DevOps et CI/CD. Autres Détails Localisation : l''équipe est principalement située en Ile-de-France avec des déplacements occasionnels à Lyon et Bruxelles. Durée de mission : Plus d’un an (maximum 3 ans) Télétravail : 50%','','2026-09-12T06:15:00+00:00','2026-09-13T06:15:00+00:00',NULL,'seen',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "mission_offers" VALUES('emagine','319188','Développeur IOS Confirmé (h/f)','https://portal.emagine.org/jobs/180137',NULL,'Lyon, France',NULL,NULL,'Hybrid','> 12 mois','ASAP','Résumé Emagine recherche pour son client final grand compte, un(e) Développeur(euse) IOS afin d’intégrer une équipe d’innovation, dans le secteur monétique. Responsabilités : Écrire un code propre et sécurisé selon les principes de Clean Architecture. Produire un code réutilisable. Guider les nouveaux développeurs et fournir un support technique. Créer ou concevoir des prototypes exploitables. Adopter des standards modernes de développement. Veiller à l''efficacité des normes et outils de conception. Collaborer et partager ses connaissances. Explorer des solutions créatives face aux défis. Maintenir une documentation complète du développement logiciel. Collaborer avec d''autres spécialistes IT. Must Haves : 5 ans d''expérience en développement mobile (Swift et SwiftUI) avec UIKit. Maîtrise des concepts de développement assisté par IA. Expérience avec Git/GitLab. Compétence avec l''outillage iOS moderne (XCode, SPM, Fastlane, Firebase, SonarQube). Connaissance des outils de CI/CD. Confortable en anglais, à l''oral et à l''écrit. Aptitudes pédagogiques pour intégrer les nouveaux collègues. Autres Détails : Démarrage : Octobre 2026 Localisation : Lyon 2 jours de télétravail par semaine','','2026-09-12T06:15:00+00:00','2026-09-13T06:15:00+00:00',NULL,'seen',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "mission_offers" VALUES('emagine','319055','Senior Manager Data Science','https://portal.emagine.org/jobs/180136',NULL,'Lisbon, Portugal',NULL,NULL,'Hybrid','Poste permanent','ASAP','At our Global Data & Analytics Hub, we prioritize collaboration, innovation, and delivering exceptional value to our customers through impactful data products. Join us to develop data capabilities that enable data-driven decisions using classical and advanced machine learning technologies. This role involves individual contributions as well as managing and coordinating a team of Data Scientists to drive business solutions. Main Responsibilities: Lead the Data Science team, coaching and supporting their development to establish a well-balanced internal and external resource team. Build analytical capabilities through individual contributions and coaching within a Product-Based Organization. Ensure effective allocation of resources for prioritized analytics projects adhering to agile principles. Managing budgeting, governance, and processes effectively. Stay updated with industry standards, integrating new technologies, algorithms, and frameworks. Key Requirements: 7+ years of experience in Data Science with a proven record of leading Data Science teams. Proficiency with AWS stack, LLMs, and Agentic Frameworks, such as LangChain. Experience in MLOps, specifically in deploying and maintaining production models, AWS SageMaker knowledge is a plus. Understanding of data governance, privacy, security, and compliance issues. Familiarity with agile methodologies and hypothesis-driven approaches. Fluent in English, both spoken and written, with strong presentation skills. Nice to Have: Knowledge of advanced data analytics techniques and tools. Experience with big data technologies.','','2026-09-12T06:15:00+00:00','2026-09-13T06:15:00+00:00',NULL,'seen',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "mission_offers" VALUES('emagine','319186','Senior Platform Engineer','https://portal.emagine.org/jobs/180135',NULL,'Poland',NULL,NULL,'Remote','4-6 mois','ASAP','Summary: The role of the Senior Platform Engineer focuses on designing, building, and operating secure and scalable cloud platforms using Google Cloud Platform (GCP). The objective is to enhance platform automation, improve operational excellence, and facilitate a seamless developer experience while ensuring compliance and security. Responsibilities: Design, build, and maintain scalable platform services and cloud infrastructure in GCP. Develop and manage Infrastructure as Code (IaC) using Terraform. Build and maintain CI/CD pipelines using GitHub Actions. Develop and maintain platform services and APIs using Python and FastAPI. Manage and optimize PostgreSQL environments and platform integrations. Ensure high availability, observability, reliability, and security of platform services. Collaborate with engineers and product teams to improve developer experience and platform adoption. Implement and maintain cloud governance, access controls, and security best practices. Monitor, troubleshoot, and resolve platform and infrastructure issues. Drive automation initiatives to reduce operational overhead and improve service quality. Support networking, connectivity, and identity management across cloud environments. Key Requirements: Bachelor''s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience. Proven experience as a Platform Engineer, DevOps Engineer, Site Reliability Engineer, or similar role. Strong experience with Python development. Hands-on experience with FastAPI or similar backend frameworks. Strong knowledge of PostgreSQL administration, performance tuning, and integrations. Extensive experience working with Google Cloud Platform (GCP). Solid experience with Terraform and Infrastructure as Code practices. Experience building and maintaining CI/CD pipelines using GitHub Actions. Strong understanding of DevOps, SRE, and platform engineering principles. Experience designing secure, scalable, and maintainable cloud architectures. Strong troubleshooting, analytical, and problem-solving skills. Excellent communication and collaboration skills. Nice to Have: Kubernetes (highly valued). Experience operating applications and platforms on Kubernetes. Metadata and data governance platforms such as OpenMetadata. GCP Networking: Load Balancers, DNS, TLS/SSL Certificates, Identity-Aware Proxy (IAP). Cloud security and networking fundamentals. Observability and monitoring tooling. Other Details: Period from: 2026-10-01 Period to: 2027-09-30 Technical Stack Required: Python, FastAPI, PostgreSQL, Google Cloud Platform (GCP), BigQuery, IAM, Pub/Sub, Cloud Run, Dataplex, Terraform, GitHub Actions. Required cloud certification: No','','2026-09-12T06:15:00+00:00','2026-09-13T06:15:00+00:00',NULL,'seen',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "mission_offers" VALUES('emagine','319185','Experienced and driven Product Designer','https://portal.emagine.org/jobs/180134',NULL,'Stockholm, Sweden',NULL,NULL,'Hybrid','4-6 mois','ASAP','Our client is looking for an experienced and driven Product Designer for an assignment starting as soon as possible and running until April 2027. The main focus will be CDT (Central Data Test Tool) , a vital tool in their pre-sales process. CDT is currently being redesigned for the future, including use across multiple brands within the Group. The solution is transitioning from a remote desktop-based application to a modern web application, creating an excellent opportunity to shape the future user experience and user interface. You will work closely with engaged users, the Product Owner and the development team. Your responsibilities will include: Translating user needs into clear user flows and designs Creating and testing concepts and prototypes Gathering feedback and continuously iterating on the solution Change management and contributing to a smooth transition to new ways of working Driving the UX/UI work forward in a complex and information-intensive domain The CDT user group is relatively small, highly engaged and significantly affected by the solution, meaning that your work will have a direct and visible impact . The development team consists of three experienced developers — two backend developers and one frontend developer — who are currently dedicating 50% of their time to the project. A Product Designer has established the initial foundations during the previous phase of the project. We are now entering an important phase of close collaboration with users, with frequent feedback loops and continuous adjustments based on real user insights. We are looking for someone who learns quickly, asks the right questions and is comfortable taking ownership of the UX/UI work . You are creative, visionary and confident in helping drive change . Strong proficiency in Figma, including design and prototyping, is required. Experience from large industrial companies or complex, information-intensive systems is advantageous. Swedish language skills are also beneficial. Start/end: Asap - 6 months Workplace: South of Stockholm - 2-3 days on site.','','2026-09-12T06:15:00+00:00','2026-09-13T06:15:00+00:00',NULL,'seen',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "mission_offers" VALUES('emagine','319166','Senior UX/UI Designer (Short-Term Project)','https://portal.emagine.org/jobs/180133',NULL,'Portugal',NULL,NULL,'Remote','1-3 mois','ASAP','Summary: The Senior UI/UX Designer is responsible for the end-to-end user experience and visual identity of an online sports betting platform, ensuring a seamless journey for players from registration to betting and withdrawals. They aim to enhance user engagement and trust while adhering to design and regulatory standards. Responsibilities: Design the core player journeys end to end: onboarding, OTP, KYC, deposit, withdrawal, bet placement, and support. Produce user flows, wireframes, prototypes, and high-fidelity screens for various platforms. Design back-office interfaces with the same rigor as player-facing screens. Build and govern the design system including guidelines and accessibility rules. Plan user research and synthesize findings into actionable recommendations. Analyze metrics and design experiments to optimize user conversions and retention. Collaborate with agile teams and validate design implementations. Embed responsible gambling features into user experiences. Act as the design authority, coaching junior designers and maintaining design processes. Must Haves: Bachelor''s or Master''s degree in design or related field. Minimum 10 years of UI/UX product design experience. Proven track record of designing transactional products that improve conversion and retention. Expert command of Figma. Strong visual design skills including typography and layout. Solid understanding of front-end technologies. Experience building and governing a design system. Nice to Haves: Experience in online betting or iGaming industry. Mobile money and payment flow design experience. Skills in motion design and micro-animations. Familiarity with design-to-code workflows. French Other Details: Experience Level: Minimum 10 years Engagement: 3-month mission','','2026-09-12T06:15:00+00:00','2026-09-13T06:15:00+00:00',NULL,'seen',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "mission_offers" VALUES('emagine','319180','Senior Cobol Software Engineer','https://portal.emagine.org/jobs/180132',NULL,'Warsaw, Poland',NULL,NULL,'Hybrid','> 12 mois','ASAP','We are seeking your support for the role of Senior Cobol Software Engineer in the Payments domain. What we offer: Long Term B2B Contract Rate: 150-190 PLN/ h + VAT ( depends of salary) Hybrid mode: 3 days from office and 2 days from home Main Responsibilities: Collaborating closely with software engineers, the product owner, business analyst, and team architect. Managing daily operations and governance of systems. Conducting testing, technical design, and analysis of user stories and reported defects. Supporting testing through troubleshooting and defect resolution. Refining new user stories while assessing their technical feasibility and design. Key Requirements: Hands-on experience with COBOL, CICS, IBM Developer for z/OS (IDz), PUMA, MQ, DB2, JCL, Git, Bitbucket, Jira, and ServiceNow. A university degree, ideally in information technology, computer science, or a closely related discipline. Proven ability to take ownership of senior software engineering tasks, delivering according to project plans and mentoring less experienced team members. Ability to successfully complete complex tasks. Strong collaboration skills, including knowledge sharing and active participation in team objectives. Fluency in written and spoken English to collaborate effectively with colleagues in Poland and Denmark. Nice to Have: Knowledge of the financial sector, particularly in banking platforms related to payments and accounts. Familiarity with microservice architecture. Experience in Java development. Experience with test automation.','','2026-09-12T06:15:00+00:00','2026-09-13T06:15:00+00:00',NULL,'seen',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "mission_offers" VALUES('emagine','319184','Senior Data Analyst','https://portal.emagine.org/jobs/180131',NULL,'Stockholm Metropolitan Area, Sweden',NULL,NULL,'Hybrid','4-6 mois','ASAP','We are seeking a highly skilled Senior Data Analyst to cover a parental leave within the Media industry. Start: ASAP, 4 month contract +/- Location: Stockholm, hybrid Main Responsibilities: Conduct independent analyses and take ownership of projects. Collaborate with team members to provide analytical support. Design experiments and statistical models. Utilize SQL and dbt for data manipulation. Integrate findings with editorial and business objectives. Key Requirements: Ability to work independently, take ownership, and provide support to others. At least five years of experience in similar roles or equivalent competence. Advanced knowledge of SQL, dbt . Experience with Snowflake is beneficial. Familiarity with analytics tools. Strong proficiency in statistical analysis, data modeling, and experiment design. Experience with Python or a similar programming language. Experience in agentic development is a significant advantage. Strong communication and stakeholder management skills. Ability to connect data insights to editorial, product, and business goals. Experience in the media industry is very advantageous. Other Details: This position is hybrid and based in Stockholm for a duration of approximately four months.','','2026-09-12T06:15:00+00:00','2026-09-13T06:15:00+00:00',NULL,'seen',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "mission_offers" VALUES('emagine','319175','D365 F&O Data Migration Analyst','https://portal.emagine.org/jobs/180130',NULL,'Poland',NULL,NULL,'Remote','> 12 mois','ASAP','The main purpose of the D365 F&O Data Migration Analyst role is to support the migration of multiple legal entities into a shared Microsoft Dynamics 365 Finance & Operations environment, ensuring data integrity and usability throughout the process. Main Responsibilities: Analyze source-system data and determine its representation in D365 F&O. Define source-to-target mappings, including transformation rules and filters. Profile source data, identify data-quality issues, and document migration risks. Prepare, execute, and troubleshoot data loads using the D365 F&O Data Management Framework. Analyze and distinguish between data, configuration, and application errors. Create validation checks and reports to ensure migrated data accuracy. Support migration rehearsals and post-go-live activities. Collaborate with functional consultants, developers, and business analysts. Analyze and migrate production, manufacturing, and inventory data. Key requirements: Bachelor’s degree or equivalent experience. Strong knowledge of Microsoft Dynamics 365 Finance & Operations. Experience with D365 F&O data management and migrations. Advanced SQL skills and experience with complex datasets. Understanding of D365 F&O data entities, legal entities and staging errors. Nice to have: Experience with ETL tools and technologies such as Azure Data Factory. Experience in D365 F&O production and manufacturing contexts. Clear communication skills with technical and non-technical stakeholders.','','2026-09-12T06:15:00+00:00','2026-09-13T06:15:00+00:00',NULL,'seen',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
